      "text": "Given the equations:\n1. \\( ab + bc + cd + da = 30 \\)\n2. \\( b + d = 5 \\)\n\nWe need to find the value of \\( a + c \\).\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the first equation by grouping terms involving \\( b \\) and \\( d \\):\n\\[ ab + bc + cd + da = (ab + da) + (bc + cd) \\]\n\nNotice that:\n\\[ ab + da = a(b + d) \\]\n\\[ bc + cd = c(b + d) \\]\n\nSo, the equation becomes:\n\\[ a(b + d) + c(b + d) = (a + c)(b + d) \\]\n\nGiven \\( b + d = 5 \\), we substitute this into the equation:\n\\[ (a + c)(b + d) = (a + c) \\cdot 5 \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ 5(a + c) = 30 \\]\n\nTo find \\( a + c \\), we divide both sides by 5:\n\\[ a + c = \\frac{30}{5} \\]\n\\[ a + c = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( a + c \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6} \\]",
